Steve Witham:
> I think you should say right at the beginning that there are small-e
> extropians, a circle of people, and there is capital-E Extropianism, a
> philosophy articulated by one of us, 

Extropianism is the work of several people, and evolving, so
I'm not sure we can define any single person as "the" Extropian.
Presumably it's reasonable to refer to those of us who are members
of the Extropy Institute, even if we don't share all of the
philosophical views of the president or directors, as
"capital-E" Extropians.  However, even as a member I prefer
the small-e, to indicate that my beliefs are more like a field 
of intellectual endeavor (like "objectivism", "science", or
"engineering") than a religion (like "Objectivism" or "Islam").

