>Has there ever been a fuzzy version of Axelrod's Iterated Prisoner's
>Dilemma tournament?  By "fuzzy", I mean with choices and scores
>not restricted to defect (0) and cooperate (1), but including all
>real numbers between.  The scoring function could be=20
>	a - bx + cy + dxy
>For Axelrod's PD, a=3Db=3D1, c=3D4, d=3D-1.

We can rewrite this payoff function (without loss of generality) as:
  J1 =3D c1u1 + c2u2 + c3u1u2

Another (more beautiful?) possibility might be:
  J1 =3D c1u1^2 + c2u2^2 + c3u1u2

If we instead of discrete iterations allow continuos time steps, we
only have to solve the problem
     /T
max (| J1 dt)
     /0
